course: dictionary
lesson: 6493
title: Nearby and close by
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Nearby means not far away, close to here or close to a place. When you meet it, look at the words around it for clues. «A seal pup alone on a beach is usually not lost: its mother may be fishing nearby.» The mother is not far off, just close by in the sea, so nearby means close.
explain: Nearby can work as two kinds of word. Before a noun it is an adjective, as in a nearby park. After a verb it is an adverb, as in we live nearby. To check the meaning, swap in close to here and see if the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Nearby is useful when you are safe. In a shop or on a trip, a nearby adult or a nearby shop is the place to ask for help. «Phones and messages nearby make homework take much longer» shows that nearby can also describe things that are close to you, not only places.
fact: Nearby means not far away, close to here or close to a place.
fact: As an adjective, nearby comes before a noun: a nearby park, a nearby friend.
fact: As an adverb, nearby comes after a verb: we live nearby.
fact: «Raccoons were brought to Europe and some escaped; now they live wild in Germany and are spreading to nearby countries.» Here nearby means close in distance.
fact: In safety, know a nearby safe place or a nearby adult you can go to for help.
exercise: «A seal pup alone on a beach is usually not lost: its mother may be fishing nearby.» What does nearby mean here? | Inside the house | Very far, over the sea | Lost and hungry | * Not far away
exercise: «We live nearby.» Is nearby an adjective or an adverb here? | Noun, because it names a place | Verb, because it shows an action | Adjective, because it comes before a noun | * Adverb, because it comes after a verb
exercise: Which sentence uses nearby as an adjective, before a noun? | We live nearby. | Let's walk nearby. | * There is a nearby shop.
test: «Raccoons were brought to Europe and some escaped; now they live wild in Germany and are spreading to nearby countries.» What does nearby mean? | Empty and quiet | * Close in distance | Far across the sea | Very old
test: You are lost in a big town. What is a sensible first step? | Walk into the road | Hide under a bench | Walk far away from everyone | * Stay where you are or go to a nearby shop and ask staff
exam: «A cosy bed nearby and a calm voice help it settle over a few nights.» Which word tells you where the bed is? | Cosy | Settle | Calm | * Nearby
